# SPIACE genome table — T11 STANDING teddy (voxel-muscle gait, CA-native movement)
# The CANONICAL teddy: SDXL-Turbo image (ambient-lit) -> TRELLIS (res 512,
# ambient capture) -> voxelize_teddy.py at H=28 (derived: canon proportions
# put the eye at H*0.45/6 cells; an eye needs >= 2 cells to exist -> H>=26.7)
# -> shape_train.py (1 pillar, margin -3.081 -> +3.100). Replaces the T1
# teddy, whose SOURCE was a mutated TRELLIS blob (measured: teddy_base.png
# is brown noise, not a bear) — the physics was faithfully animating a bad
# statue. vmStride/vmLift are the T4-trained pair; they may re-train at this
# scale (the leg budget derivation is scale-relative), T9 measures first.

kind           = vox
genome         = teddy-stand-muscle-v1
embodiment     = 1
tickMs         = 30
cell           = 0.06
cellsFile      = teddy_stand_s1.cells
vmGait         = 1
vmStride       = 2
vmLift         = 1

# --- B4: FK/IK rig (INERT under vmGait — kept for the loader) --------------
b4A            = 2
b4T            = 60
b4Lam          = 12.25
b4Dth          = 0.08
b4ThMax        = 2.6
b4Iters        = 5

# --- N5: physics membrane (SI in, sim units derived) ------------------------
gravity        = 9.81
tickHz         = 60
